      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5e4ca2145f9b3726b3b389e7|full_name} Yes. I know about multipass rendering in Shader and many toon shader draw meshes twice for drawing outline(I forgot I read that in which shader, UTS or Arktoon?).\n\nI don't think there's any need to count multi-pass rendering with shaders. I know it's technically difficult.\n\nAnyone who can write shaders can write shaders for bypass this problem. Or simply use VeryPoorAvatar.\n\nI think this problem has a small impact. so I agree that many other important problems should be solved.\n\nI encountered this problem in the \"Combining meshes with AAO(AvatarOptimizer,3rd-party avatar optimize tool) increase triangles\" case study.\n\nThis case was caused by this case is \"MeshRenderer has an additional material slot, AAO Mesh Combining worked fine, generated new sub-mesh from that additional-material-slot\".\n\nYou might wonder \"What are the use cases for additional-material-slot?\"\n\nThis article taught me, and this article have many favs , many users also mentioned it on Twitter(X).\n\nhttps://note.com/rokota/n/n8d951ff62ca4\n\nThis additional-material-slot technique acts like an AvatarPerformanceRank hack.\n\nHowever,I expect that in most cases, for Poor avatars, the increase will only be a 2 or 3 materials, or the number of rendering polygons will increase from 70,000 to 100,000.\n\nThis post was written solely to let you know that this is the case.\n\nRepeatly I think this problem has low-priority.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
